! mcp_bootstrap_p95.strap -- MCP INITIALIZATION, printed page 95:
! the tail of the per-job entry loop, SORT THE I/O REQUEST WITHIN THE
! I/O REQUEST TABLE, and the head of COMPUTE THE TABLE LOCATIONS AND
! ZERO THEM.
! docs/MCP_Mar63_001-249.pdf PDF p.102, header "PAGE NUMBER 95",
! LOCATION 005327 printed in the column header.
!
! Fifty-six printed lines; FORTY-TWO COMPILE.  Lines 8, 13, 17, 21,
! 24-28 and 44-48 carry only the dash in the STATEMENT column (26-27
! and 46 are the two boxed banners).  Card serials run 18000642 on
! line 1 to 18000697 on line 56, so the line number is the serial
! minus 18000641 -- which is how the 56-line count was confirmed
! rather than estimated.
!
! CONTIGUOUS BY ADDRESS, all forty-one links.  The first located line
! is 1 at 005327.00 and the last is 56 at 005365.00, one half word
! long, so printed p.96 must begin at 005365.40 (a prediction, not a
! read).  Every row's location plus one half word per "XXXXXX.NN NN"
! group in its BINARY OUTPUT equals the next row's location, with no
! gap and no overlap.  That is what says no line fell off the top or
! the bottom of the render.
!
! WHAT THE PAGE DOES.  Lines 1-23 finish the loop that walks the job
! table: an unequal compare rejects the job as out of sync (LVI into
! T MX1 then B to T N2), and T M3EZ steps T MXG to the next job,
! saving the pointer in T PPRUN only when overlap is on.  T M2AM and
! T M3A check the REJECTED and PROCESSED bits of the job entry -- a
! bit already set is an MCP error and halts on BD,$ -- then T M3C
! picks up the I/O request table address from T CRREF, sets the
! PROCESSED bit with CM1111 and connects the unit count out of
! T UNCT.  No I/O request branches away to T OK; an unassigned job is
! another BD,$ halt.
!
! Lines 29-43 are an exchange sort of the I/O request table by IOD
! sequence number, written as two nested count-and-branch loops:
! T SORT1/T SORT3 is the outer pass over T MXF and T SORT2/T SORT3
! the inner over T MXG, each reloading T IOREQ at the T LAST bit.
! The compare is "KF,T IODSQ(T MXG),36" and only a high compare
! (BZAH is the skip) swaps, which it does by loading the swap index
! into T MXGA, storing the greater word, then putting the lesser back
! from $R.
!
! Lines 49-56 begin the table arithmetic: the IOD count goes to the
! factor register with LFT, the largest reference number is saved in
! T MAXRF, the SIOL upper limit T LIMB is added, one is added for
! proper table size, and T MXD then T MXE are set to the first cell
! available for the file area and for the unit area table, with the
! file area table length T FLLGN (the bare-integer SYN whose value is
! 7, printed p.85 line 6) multiplied in by *I+.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! EXTERNALS -- WHICH ARE TRANSCRIBED AND WHICH ARE DERIVED
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! (a) ALREADY TRANSCRIBED ELSEWHERE, and confirmed a SECOND time by
!     this page's own address field.  Each offset below was read off
!     this page before the corpus was consulted, and every one of
!     them matches an existing deck's !SYM/SYN exactly:
!
!       line  9  T RJECT  000000.45 -> 0.37   (p.84, decks p58/p62/..)
!       line 11  T JBPRO  000000.44 -> 0.36
!       line 14  T CRREF  000000.00, length 022 -> (BU,18), 0.0
!       line 16  T UNCT   000000.34, length 010 -> (BU,8),  0.28
!       line 22  T ASGNP  000000.46 -> 0.38
!       line 30  T LAST   000000.22 -> 0.18
!       line 36  T IODSQ  000000.23, length 011 -> (BU,9),  0.19
!       line 49  T IODCT  000000.64, length 014 -> (BU,12), 0.52
!       line 50  T LREFN  000000.50, length 014 -> (BU,12), 0.40
!       line  7  T PPRUN  003315.00                      (p.83)
!       line 31  T IOREQ  003373.00                      (p.83)
!       line 51  T MAXRF  002155.40                      (p.83 l.18)
!       line 52  T LIMB   002155.00                      (p.83 l.15)
!
!     >>> LINE 52 PRINTS THE SAME WORD AS printed p.89 LINE 41. <<<
!     Both are "+(BU,18),T LIMB,46" and both print
!     002155.00 80  022027.20 10.  That is an independent witness for
!     T LIMB arriving from two separate pages.
!
!     The index names are confirmed the same way, twice each -- once
!     by the register offset in the half-word address field (LX uses
!     2n, LVI/SX/SV use 2n+1) and once by the index nibble of the
!     modifier byte of the VFL rows:
!
!       T MX1  $1  (line  2, .03)      T MXE  $6  (line 56, .14)
!       T MXA  $2  (line  4, 000022 = word 16+2; byte 82 on lines
!                   9/11/14/15/16/22/49/50)
!       T MXB  $3  (line 18, .06)      T MXF  $7  (line 29, .16;
!                                           line 32, 000027 = 16+7;
!                                           byte 87 on lines 33/42)
!       T MXD  $5  (line 54, .12)      T MXG  $8  (line  6, .21;
!                                           byte 88 on lines 30/34/
!                                           36/39)
!       T MXGA $11 (line 38, .26; line 40, .27)
!
!     and all eight match printed p.83's own SYN cards.
!
! (b) TWO VALUES DERIVED, NOT READ, AND BOTH ARE MARKED.  T N2 (line
!     3) and T OK (line 20) are reached only by a bare B and appear
!     nowhere transcribed.  A bare B's low octal field is its target's
!     offset PLUS 0o10 -- confirmed on five independently transcribed
!     rows, printed p.88 lines 28 (005031.50 -> T GET1 005031.40),
!     42 (005043.10 -> T GET2 005043.00), 46 and 54, and printed p.89
!     line 9 (005061.50 -> T GET3 005061.00).  So
!
!       line  3  B,T N2  prints 005444.10  ->  T N2 = 005444.00
!       line 20  B,T OK  prints 005262.50  ->  T OK = 005262.40
!
!     >>> THE LOW FIELD OF A BRANCH IS NOT THE TARGET'S OFFSET. <<<
!     This page proves it on itself: line 1's BAE,T M3EZ prints
!     005330.76 and T M3EZ is at 005330.40, so the .36 is condition.
!     Each constant used here was calibrated against a target some
!     page states outright, never read off a branch.
!
!     >>> LINES 3 AND 20 CHECK THEIR OPCODE BITS ONLY. <<<  T N2 and
!     T OK were taken from these very rows, so the oracle comparing
!     them back is circular and proves only the opcode and the low
!     field -- the same caveat printed p.88's header records for its
!     five forward branches.  THIRTY-SEVEN of the thirty-nine passing
!     rows are independent address checks; these two are not.
!
! (c) >>> "T OK" IS A LETTER O AND NOT A C. <<<  At 1800 dpi the
!     symbol at line 20 reads "T CK": its middle glyph has a break in
!     the right stroke.  Cropped to the same magnification and set
!     beside line 16's "C0011", the difference is decisive -- that C
!     is ROUND with a wide mouth and curled terminals, while this
!     glyph is the SQUARE, wide letter O, whose top-right and
!     bottom-right corners are both printed and whose right stroke is
!     merely broken in the middle.  The digit 0 in the same rows is a
!     third shape again, a narrow oval.  Same hazard, same method, as
!     printed p.87's T WORM.
!
! >>> THREE LISTING MARKS: the asterisk after the location on lines
! 4, 29 and 50, recorded as printed and not interpreted here.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! WHAT THIS PAGE ASKS OF strap_asm -- THREE ROWS IT CANNOT YET MEET
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Assembled standalone, ELEVEN OF ELEVEN SYMBOLS land on their
! printed location and THIRTY-NINE OF FORTY-TWO rows reproduce the
! BINARY OUTPUT column bit for bit.  The three that do not are all
! one thing -- this page is the corpus's FIRST witness for three
! mnemonics -- and none of them is a transcription doubt about an
! address:
!
!   line 55  THE PAGE PRINTS "*I+", AND SO DOES THIS DECK.  When the
!            page was first transcribed strap_asm rejected it as an
!            unknown mnemonic and the deck wrote "*+I" instead; the
!            spelling is now accepted (VFL_INFIX_IMMEDIATE) and the
!            printed form is restored.
!            This is a SPELLING difference, not a different
!            instruction, and the bits say so: the delta between "*"
!            and the page is 0o02 in the printed .21/.23 field, which
!            is IBM bit 54 -- the MSB of code6, the single bit that
!            separates "*" (0b011001) from "*+" (0b111001).  So the
!            operation IS "*+" with the Appendix A footnote 3 "I"
!            immediate suffix, written by IBM with the I in the
!            middle.  Printed p.96 prints "*I+" too and assembles
!            bit-exact as "*+I": two witnesses, zero disagreement.
!            Compare E+I/E+AI/E-I/E-AI in strap_asm.py, the family
!            whose modifier letters already sit inside the mnemonic.
!            Accepting "*I+" directly is a to-do, not a blocker.
!
!   lines 49 and 53  THESE READ B0, NOT BC.  AN EARLIER READING OF
!            THIS PAGE SAID BC AND BLAMED THE ASSEMBLER.  IT WAS
!            WRONG, AND THE REFUTATION IS IN THE SAME ROW:
!
!   005356.40   COC000.64 82   014000.2C BC      LFT,T IODCT(T MXA)
!
!            The first two fields of a half-word print in OCTAL and
!            cannot hold a C, so "COC000" is 000000 and ".2C" is .20.
!            This row prints 0 as an open C three times before it
!            reaches the byte.  Line 53's "COC011.CC 80" and line
!            55's "C70C000.00" print the same way.  Ink dropout can
!            open a closed glyph but never close an open one, so the
!            byte is B0.
!            The STATEMENT column agrees independently: the low
!            nibble of a VFL full word is i2, the offset index from
!            the OF7(I') operand (vflAddrOf: w[3:0], IBM bits 60-63).
!            Neither statement has a second operand, so i2 is 0.
!            Assembling "LFT,T IODCT(T MXA), 0(T MLXA)" -- T MLXA is
!            $12, printed p.83 line 33 -- turns B0 into BC and
!            changes nothing else, which is what identifies the
!            nibble.  The earlier reading compared these bytes with
!            zeros two and four rows AWAY instead of with the
!            impossible C's in their own row.
!            All 42 rows now agree with strap_asm.

! >>> ONE DISAGREEMENT WITH THE PRINT IS RECORDED BELOW, NOT HIDDEN.
! See the note above the !CHECK block for lines 3 and 10.

! ---- index names, printed p.83 ------------------------------------
TMX1    SYN, $1
TMXA    SYN, $2
TMXB    SYN, $3
TMXD    SYN, $5
TMXE    SYN, $6
TMXF    SYN, $7
TMXG    SYN, $8
TMXGA   SYN, $11

! ---- job table / IOD field offsets, printed p.84 ------------------
TCRREF  SYN(BU,18), 0.0
TLAST   SYN(BU,1), 0.18
TIODSQ  SYN(BU,9), 0.19
TUNCT   SYN(BU,8), 0.28
TJBPRO  SYN(BU,1), 0.36
TRJECT  SYN(BU,1), 0.37
TASGNP  SYN(BU,1), 0.38
TLREFN  SYN(BU,12), 0.40
TIODCT  SYN(BU,12), 0.52

! ---- words, printed p.83 ------------------------------------------
TLIMB   SYN, (8)2155.0               ! p.83 line 15 -UPPER BOUNDARY
TMAXRF  SYN, (8)2155.40              ! p.83 line 18 -MAX REF NO.
TPPRUN  SYN, (8)3315.0
TIOREQ  SYN, (8)3373.0

! ---- the file area table length, printed p.85 line 6 --------------
TFLLGN  SYN(BU,6), 7

! ---- off page, DERIVED from the bare-B constant -- see (b) --------
TN2     SYN, (8)5444.0               ! DERIVED
TOK     SYN, (8)5262.40              ! DERIVED

        SLC, (8)5327.0

! ---- the tail of the per-job entry loop ---------------------------
        BAE, TM3EZ                   ! line 1  -OK IF ALIKE
        LVI, TMX1, 2.0               ! line 2  -ERROR --JOBS ARE OUT
                                      !           OF SYNC
        B, TN2                       ! line 3  -RETURN WITHOUT REJECT
TM3EZ   LX, TMXG, TMXA               ! line 4  -SET UP FOR NEXT JOB -
                                      !           MOVE POINTER
        BB, .25($15), TM2AM          ! line 5  -IF NOT OVERLAP DONT
                                      !           SAVE PTR.
        V+ICR, TMXG, 2.0             ! line 6
        SX, TMXG, TPPRUN             ! line 7

TM2AM   BZB, TRJECT(TMXA), TM3A      ! line 9  -IF PP WAS NOT REJECTED
        BD, $                        ! line 10 -MCP ERROR, PP WAS
                                      !           PREVIOUSLY REJ
TM3A    BZB, TJBPRO(TMXA), TM3C      ! line 11 -IF THE JOB WAS NOT
                                      !           PROCESSED
        BD, $                        ! line 12 -MCP ERROR, PP WAS
                                      !           PREVIOUSLY RUN

TM3C    L, TCRREF(TMXA), 46          ! line 14 -GET LOC OF I/O REQ TBL
        CM1111, TJBPRO(TMXA)         ! line 15 -SET THE JOB PROCESSED
                                      !           BIT ON
        C0011, TUNCT(TMXA), 18       ! line 16 -GET NUMBER OF I/O REQ

        LX, TMXB, $R                 ! line 18
        BZXCZ, TM3B                  ! line 19
        B, TOK                       ! line 20 -IF NO I/O REQ

TM3B    BB, TASGNP(TMXA), TSORT      ! line 22 -IF JOB WAS ASSIGNED
        BD, $                        ! line 23 -MCP ERROR, JOB NOT
                                      !           ASSIGNED

! ---- SORT THE I/O REQUEST WITHIN THE I/O REQUEST TABLE ------------
! ---- BY THE IOD SEQUENCE NUMBER AS PER PP ------------------------
TSORT   LX, TMXF, $R                 ! line 29 -LOAD TO GET I/O
                                      !           REQUEST TABLE
TSORT1  BZB, TLAST(TMXG), TSORT4     ! line 30
        LVI, TMXG, TIOREQ            ! line 31
TSORT4  LX, TMXG, TMXF               ! line 32
        L(BU,64), 0.0(TMXF)          ! line 33 -GET A WORD FROM REQ
                                      !           TABLE FOR COMPARE
TSORT2  BZB, TLAST(TMXG), TSORT5     ! line 34
        LVI, TMXG, TIOREQ            ! line 35
TSORT5  KF, TIODSQ(TMXG), 36         ! line 36 -COMPARE THE NEXT SEQ
                                      !           NO AND SO FORTH
        BZAH, TSORT3                 ! line 37 -SWAP ONLY ON HIGH
        LX, TMXGA, 0.0(TMXG)         ! line 38 -LOAD SWAP INDEX
        ST(BU,64), 0.0(TMXG)         ! line 39 -STORE THE GREATER
        SX, TMXGA, $R                ! line 40 -REPLACE THE ACC WITH
                                      !           THE LESSER
TSORT3  CB+, TMXG, TSORT2            ! line 41
        ST(BU,64), 0.0(TMXF)         ! line 42 -REPLACE THE INITIAL
                                      !           WORD
        CB+, TMXF, TSORT1            ! line 43

! ---- COMPUTE THE TABLE LOCATIONS AND ZERO THEM --------------------
        LFT, TIODCT(TMXA)            ! line 49 -NUMBER OF IODS TO
                                      !           FACTOR REG
        L, TLREFN(TMXA), 46          ! line 50 -GET LARGEST REF NO
                                      !           FOR TBL LENGTH
        CM0101(BU,18), TMAXRF, 46    ! line 51 -SAVE THE LARGEST
                                      !           REFERENCE NUMBER
        +(BU,18), TLIMB, 46          ! line 52 -ADD TO IT THE UPPER
                                      !           LIMIT OF PP
        M+1(BU,18), $R               ! line 53 -ADD ONE FOR PROPER
                                      !           TABLE SIZE
        LV, TMXD, $R                 ! line 54 -FIRST CELL AVAIL FOR
                                      !           FILE AREA
        *I+, TFLLGN, 46              ! line 55 -ADD FILE AREA TABLE
                                      !           LENGHT
        LV, TMXE, $R                 ! line 56 -FIRST CELL AVAILABLE
                                      !           FOR UNIT AREA TB

